# Server-side rendering of view pages: the document, escaping of every
# dynamic value, metadata layering, @Load serialization into k-data, and
# failed loads with their status (docs/compiler/server.md §7,
# docs/compiler/runtime.md §6, docs/design/14-async-data.md, 22-metadata.md).
#
# Expectations are written against the markers of runtime.md §6: a dynamic
# text alone in an element renders without markers, so `>Article intro</h1>`
# is matched without the opening tag.

### a page renders a complete HTML document
GET /plain
>>> 200
content-type: text/html; charset=utf-8
x-content-type-options: nosniff
~ <!doctype html>
~ <html lang="en">
~ <head>
~ </head>
~ <body>
~ plain page
~ </html>

### the document links the hashed stylesheet and module scripts
GET /plain
>>> 200
~ <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/
~ <script type="module" src="/assets/

### the document carries the hydration data element
GET /plain
>>> 200
~ <script type="application/json" id="k-data">
~ "v":1
~ "session":{"user":null}

### rendering a page for a guest sets no cookie
GET /plain
>>> 200
!set-cookie

### the layout wraps the page
GET /plain
>>> 200
~ site header
~ <main>

### the layout's metadata applies when the page has none
GET /plain
>>> 200
~ <title>SSR Test</title>
~ <meta name="description" content="The layout&#39;s description.">

### @NoLayout renders the page without the default layout
GET /bare
>>> 200
~ bare page
!~ site header

### HEAD of a page has the GET status and headers and no body
HEAD /plain
>>> 200
content-type: text/html; charset=utf-8
=

### a default parameter renders its default
GET /greeting
>>> 200
~ Hello, world
~ <title>Hello world</title>

### a link to the page at its default parameter omits it from the query
GET /greeting
>>> 200
~ href="/greeting"

### a query parameter is decoded before rendering
GET /greeting?name=%C3%A9t%C3%A9
>>> 200
~ Hello, été

### text from a parameter is escaped in the body
GET /greeting?name=%3Cb%3Ebold%3C%2Fb%3E
>>> 200
~ Hello, &lt;b&gt;bold&lt;/b&gt;
!~ <b>bold

### text from a parameter is escaped in the title
GET /greeting?name=%3Cb%3E
>>> 200
~ <title>Hello &lt;b&gt;</title>

### an attribute from a parameter escapes quotes as well
GET /greeting?name=%22%3E%3Cimg%20src%3Dx%3E%27
>>> 200
~ alt="A wave for &quot;&gt;&lt;img src=x&gt;&#39;"
!~ "><img src=x>

### an ampersand is escaped in text
GET /greeting?name=a%26b
>>> 200
~ Hello, a&amp;b

### a link built from a parameter percent-encodes it in the href
GET /greeting?name=%3Cb%3E
>>> 200
~ href="/greeting?name=%3Cb%3E"

### the page's @Load values render in the view
GET /articles/intro
>>> 200
~ >Article intro</h1>
~ Body of intro &amp; more

### a dependent load runs after the load it reads
GET /articles/intro
>>> 200
~ intro-a
~ intro-b

### the loaded values are serialized into k-data for hydration
# k-data escapes <, > and & as \uXXXX (docs/compiler/runtime.md §11).
GET /articles/intro
>>> 200
~ "loads":{
~ "article":{"slug":"intro","title":"Article intro","body":"Body of intro \u0026 more"}
~ "related":["intro-a","intro-b"]

### the loading block is not rendered once the loads resolved
GET /articles/intro
>>> 200
!~ Loading article

### the page's metadata overrides the layout's
GET /articles/intro
>>> 200
~ <title>Article intro · SSR Test</title>
~ <meta name="description" content="Read Article intro">
!~ The layout&#39;s description.

### canonical renders the page's absolute URL from the public origin
GET /articles/intro
>>> 200
~ <link rel="canonical" href="http://localhost/articles/intro">

### a canonical URL built from a parameter is encoded and escaped
GET /articles/a%22b
>>> 200
~ <link rel="canonical" href="http://localhost/articles/a%22b">

### loaded markup is escaped in the view and the title
GET /articles/xss
>>> 200
~ &lt;script&gt;alert(1)&lt;/script&gt;
~ <title>&lt;script&gt;alert(1)&lt;/script&gt; · SSR Test</title>
!~ <script>alert

### a script end tag in loaded data can't close the k-data element
GET /articles/xss
>>> 200
~ \u003c/script\u003e\u003cscript\u003ealert(2)\u003c/script\u003e
!~ </script><script>alert(2)

### a path parameter is percent-decoded
GET /articles/a%20b
>>> 200
~ >Article a b</h1>

### an encoded slash stays inside one path parameter
GET /articles/a%2Fb
>>> 200
~ >Article a/b</h1>

### an empty path segment doesn't match a String parameter
GET /articles/
>>> 404

### a failed load with status(.notFound) answers 404
GET /articles/missing
>>> 404
content-type: text/html; charset=utf-8
~ No such article

### the failed block's metadata replaces the page's, which isn't evaluated
GET /articles/missing
>>> 404
~ <title>Not found · SSR Test</title>
!~ Read

### status(.forbidden) in failed answers 403 with the layout's title
GET /articles/hidden
>>> 403
~ This article is hidden.
~ <title>SSR Test</title>

### a failed block without status(_:) answers 200
GET /articles/locked
>>> 200
~ Locked until &lt;tomorrow&gt;
!~ <tomorrow>

### the typed error of a failed load is serialized for hydration
GET /articles/locked
>>> 200
~ "case":"locked"
~ "until":"\u003ctomorrow\u003e"

### a failed page is still wrapped in the layout
GET /articles/missing
>>> 404
~ site header

### a load that panics is a 500
GET /broken
>>> 500
!~ <script type="application/json" id="k-data">

### an unknown path is a 404 page
GET /no-such-page
>>> 404

### the root path has no page in this app
GET /
>>> 404
